{"v":1,"id":"zgor4Xg926c","src":"segs","c":[[0,"[SIDE CONVERSATION]"],[28,"Our next speaker, Bryan Wilder, who"],[70,"is one of our machine"],[91,"learning faculty who"],[103,"will speak to us about"],[133,"some of the frontier work"],[146,"that him and his crew are"],[166,"doing on belief elicitation"],[184,"and interpretation of these models."],[206,"Bryan."],[209,"Wonderful."],[213,"Yeah, thank you for having me."],[229,"So the sequencing of the"],[236,"talks is really nice here,"],[246,"because a lot of"],[262,"motivation I don't really"],[273,"have to do anymore."],[289,"You can understand a lot of what I'm"],[302,"going to talk about"],[307,"here as exactly trying"],[327,"to flesh out the interpretationist side"],[365,"of this program for"],[377,"understanding model behavior."],[401,"And so I'm not going to talk about"],[413,"representations at all,"],[423,"though I do think it's"],[429,"very important to connect"],[448,"those perspectives."],[454,"And that's also"],[459,"something we're working on."],[488,"So one recurring example I'm going to use"],[526,"is understanding coordinated behavior."],[556,"So I also don't really have to motivate"],[576,"why we would want to do this"],[593,"or why it's an important topic."],[617,"So one thing that many people"],[639,"looking at this HuggingFace"],[650,"incident would say is that the sort of"],[669,"coordinated behavior"],[679,"is cooperative,"],[692,"agents are willing to"],[703,"sacrifice themselves"],[712,"to benefit other agents."],[726,"And so one kind of behavioral question"],[769,"that you might want to ask"],[780,"is, \"are these good descriptions?\""],[798,"Do you models behave in"],[808,"seemingly altruistic ways"],[825,"towards other models?"],[842,"What's a good description of this"],[852,"behavior that would allow us"],[863,"to predict it in the future?"],[890,"And so in addition to the"],[918,"sort of interpretationist"],[934,"explanations here of why models would do"],[962,"these kinds of things,"],[979,"I also want to contrast"],[1007,"those with explanations"],[1021,"in terms of how models are designed."],[1051,"So you could say, for example, maybe,"],[1070,"or you could hypothesize that agents"],[1093,"were trained in environments that"],[1107,"involved multi-agent coordination."],[1124,"And that's why they"],[1132,"engage in coordinated behavior."],[1152,"And that would be a"],[1156,"different kind of explanation"],[1170,"than interpretationist ones that would"],[1194,"posit that they have specific"],[1208,"kinds of desires and beliefs"],[1220,"and so on."],[1239,"And one important thing here is that"],[1268,"these are not mutually"],[1280,"exclusive kinds of explanations at all."],[1300,"Like they're just explanations at sort"],[1317,"of different levels of abstraction"],[1330,"that will be useful"],[1336,"for different purposes."],[1348,"And I could, for"],[1356,"example, say that there's"],[1368,"particular features of the design"],[1390,"environment for agents"],[1399,"that leads them to have"],[1410,"specific kinds of beliefs and desires"],[1427,"and so on."],[1441,"And so the research agenda here that I'm"],[1484,"kind of working within"],[1514,"and I'll talk about a"],[1527,"couple pieces of today"],[1543,"is to first establish empirically"],[1581,"whether these kinds of"],[1597,"intentional interpretationist"],[1610,"explanations are"],[1624,"appropriate for LLM agents."],[1649,"So I think there's some amount of"],[1658,"controversy right now,"],[1666,"even at this stage, like a lot of people"],[1681,"object to sort of anthropomorphic"],[1703,"descriptions of language"],[1721,"models and their behavior."],[1739,"But then to the extent"],[1750,"that we think that they"],[1756,"are at least useful, then to"],[1771,"develop an empirical research"],[1785,"program that allows us"],[1800,"to test and distinguish"],[1814,"different kinds of"],[1821,"interpretationist explanations."],[1857,"And then finally, to"],[1893,"connect those to explanations"],[1911,"at the level of the sort"],[1920,"of design or engineering"],[1928,"of the system, because to the extent"],[1947,"that these are engineered artifacts,"],[1959,"then we can go back and change things."],[1973,"So if we know why"],[1987,"undesired behaviors happen"],[2001,"in a way that"],[2024,"connects these sort of maybe"],[2044,"like motivational"],[2053,"roots of those behaviors"],[2067,"to features of the training environment,"],[2083,"then we have an angle to start working"],[2114,"on improving the behavior."],[2136,"So I'm going to talk"],[2146,"largely about the first two"],[2170,"components of this today."],[2191,"But this is, I think, sort of--"],[2216,"it's a much bigger agenda, obviously,"],[2231,"than I'm going to solve in a single talk."],[2251,"And I think that this is really something"],[2271,"that I want to propose the field"],[2294,"collectively should be devoting"],[2319,"a lot of attention to."],[2343,"So to start in on the"],[2356,"first component of this,"],[2383,"so what I'm going to be trying to do"],[2409,"in the first part of this talk is"],[2427,"to give us a way to"],[2447,"kind of empirically verify"],[2461,"whether some of these"],[2468,"preconditions for interpretationism"],[2494,"to be an appropriate"],[2506,"description of a system are present."],[2531,"So I guess I also don't have to motivate"],[2557,"kind of decision theoretic perspective,"],[2577,"though maybe I guess people--"],[2591,"now I know people will make"],[2598,"fun of me for setting Savage"],[2609,"instead of Jeffrey Bolker here."],[2633,"But the only sort of caveat that I"],[2663,"want to add to the way"],[2672,"that we think about coherence"],[2694,"as inducing sort of"],[2717,"interpretations of a system"],[2731,"as having beliefs and desires is that I"],[2761,"think it's useful for us to"],[2775,"distinguish between a couple"],[2792,"kinds of coherence when we were dealing"],[2808,"with language models,"],[2818,"at least heuristically."],[2833,"So one is like a kind of"],[2862,"within-context coherence."],[2878,"So in the course of a specific episode"],[2900,"where an agent is"],[2906,"solving a specific task,"],[2920,"does it act like it has"],[2940,"specific kinds of beliefs and desires"],[2957,"and so on?"],[2972,"And then the other is a broader"],[3001,"across-context sense"],[3019,"in that when I use, say, GPT to solve"],[3055,"lots of different kinds of tasks,"],[3071,"does it act like it has kind of stable"],[3094,"behavioral dispositions,"],[3114,"of beliefs and desires?"],[3133,"And the first sense is, I"],[3170,"think, kind of easier, right?"],[3189,"Because systems are getting"],[3214,"really good at solving tasks."],[3225,"They're being trained very hard to solve"],[3244,"tasks very efficiently."],[3258,"So they kind of have to start"],[3270,"having more of this first kind"],[3300,"of coherence."],[3308,"But it isn't necessarily the case"],[3332,"that that will translate as"],[3342,"much into the second kind."],[3353,"That's at least--"],[3363,"I think it's easier to"],[3373,"see why this might not"],[3395,"as strongly just out of"],[3435,"the training paradigm."],[3456,"Though I'm sure companies would also"],[3473,"like them to have a lot"],[3485,"of number two as well."],[3506,"So we should be on the"],[3517,"lookout for whether we're only"],[3545,"making inferences about"],[3554,"one or the other of these."],[3595,"So in terms of how--"],[3614,"with this kind of in"],[3629,"the back of our minds,"],[3650,"I want to ask about how we"],[3664,"should go about validating"],[3684,"descriptions of beliefs"],[3711,"or desires to a system."],[3737,"So let's talk about beliefs."],[3759,"And suppose I've looked at some of the"],[3781,"behavior of the system."],[3795,"And I infer that it"],[3807,"holds a belief Z, right?"],[3829,"So what makes that a good description"],[3858,"of the behavior of the system?"],[3886,"And what I propose here, which I don't"],[3943,"think this kind of idea"],[3962,"here is really original to me."],[3975,"Seems very consistent"],[3991,"with a lot of previous stuff"],[4000,"in the literature and"],[4008,"what was in the last talk,"],[4020,"is that there's a couple"],[4027,"of properties we want here."],[4044,"One is that it's a really"],[4070,"predictably useful description"],[4086,"that we can make good out of sample"],[4105,"predictions of behavior"],[4115,"that we have not seen from the"],[4127,"system as a result of knowing"],[4140,"that a belief Z. And then the second"],[4167,"is that that prediction should be"],[4183,"structured in a particular way."],[4200,"So there's lots of"],[4207,"predictive models that work well,"],[4225,"but it doesn't really"],[4231,"make sense to talk about them"],[4243,"as descriptions of beliefs."],[4258,"And so the other thing that we want"],[4280,"is that the way that Z"],[4299,"allows us to predict decisions"],[4312,"should be consistent with the"],[4322,"role that beliefs should play"],[4343,"in decision making on some"],[4360,"theory of rational behavior."],[4400,"So this is the components of this"],[4433,"that we've flushed out"],[4453,"over a couple of papers here."],[4478,"So the first of these was led by my PhD"],[4500,"student, Khurram Yamin,"],[4513,"who's here today."],[4524,"So you should talk to him."],[4551,"That talks about how we flesh out"],[4585,"these sort of structural properties."],[4607,"And then in a second"],[4622,"work here with Alex Smolin,"],[4641,"we basically say that,"],[4662,"OK, if we infer beliefs"],[4675,"that satisfy these"],[4683,"properties, then can we empirically"],[4698,"evaluate how predictive they are?"],[4733,"The setting in which"],[4741,"both of these works operate"],[4762,"is these kind of"],[4778,"statistical decision tasks"],[4795,"where an agent observes a context x"],[4827,"and then has to take an action a."],[4849,"And there's some true state y that they"],[4872,"don't get to observe."],[4880,"They just see x, which provides some"],[4899,"information about y."],[4921,"And so for the purposes of"],[4937,"all of our illustrations here,"],[4949,"we're going to take y to be binary"],[4965,"so that we can talk about a belief just"],[4985,"as a subjective"],[4990,"probability, like the agent's"],[5008,"subjective probability that y is 1 given"],[5030,"the context x, which"],[5044,"I'm going to write as p hat."],[5065,"So a simple example here is"],[5085,"that you look out the window"],[5098,"in the morning, you see"],[5107,"what the sky looks like."],[5117,"That's the context x."],[5133,"And then you form a"],[5155,"subjective probability"],[5168,"about whether it will rain."],[5188,"And you make a decision,"],[5198,"should I take an umbrella?"],[5216,"And then we can also compare afterwards"],[5235,"whether it actually rained."],[5267,"So within this framework, I'm going"],[5292,"to start in on this first set of work"],[5322,"here about asking how we can verify"],[5355,"whether beliefs satisfy the"],[5372,"correct format in relation"],[5392,"to decisions."],[5430,"So here is the framework"],[5445,"that we're going to operate in"],[5474,"is one where we just look at"],[5489,"the behavior from the outside"],[5503,"in kind of a black box way."],[5522,"And so we get to see many"],[5542,"samples of a decision task"],[5563,"in which I see examples of the input x."],[5591,"There's the unknown y"],[5604,"that I also observe."],[5618,"And then I elicit the LLM's report"],[5671,"of some probability p"],[5699,"hat and an action a."],[5727,"And so what I want now"],[5742,"is to be able to test"],[5756,"whether those"],[5760,"distributions are mutually coherent."],[5784,"So is the decision making compatible"],[5809,"with it being produced by"],[5828,"an agent who truly holds"],[5844,"reported belief p hat?"],[5862,"And if you don't want this"],[5887,"p hat to be a number that's"],[5895,"reported by the LLM, it could be also"],[5923,"whatever else you've"],[5931,"kind of inferred that"],[5951,"the system believes."],[5959,"You can ask, similarly,"],[5972,"is that a good description"],[5980,"in this sense?"],[6000,"And so the challenge here is to work out"],[6028,"what are the sort of testable"],[6040,"implications of holding"],[6051,"a belief in a way that"],[6071,"makes a set of assumptions"],[6085,"that we are comfortable"],[6096,"making about language models."],[6117,"And here, the right kinds of assumptions"],[6139,"might be relatively"],[6149,"different than they are for people."],[6173,"So because, for example,"],[6185,"there's this tradition of work"],[6209,"in economics, for"],[6227,"example, about belief elicitation"],[6256,"where we make assumptions"],[6264,"about utility functions."],[6276,"We say people prefer"],[6288,"having more money instead"],[6301,"of having less money."],[6312,"And so I will offer them payments"],[6339,"for which it would be utility"],[6362,"maximizing in terms of money"],[6382,"to truthfully report your belief."],[6405,"And this really seems kind of like--"],[6437,"it's not clear how you"],[6446,"should think about this"],[6451,"for language models."],[6463,"The entire exercise I'm doing this"],[6478,"would be sort of fake"],[6488,"right now to start with."],[6501,"Maybe models are willing to"],[6513,"kind of role play with you"],[6526,"and act as if they desired"],[6537,"money if you kind of suggest"],[6549,"that they should."],[6556,"And that could be one useful way to"],[6571,"explore their behavior."],[6582,"But it doesn't seem like we"],[6595,"want to pin all of our hopes"],[6610,"on that working."],[6634,"So we don't want to--"],[6647,"for the purposes of this work, we're"],[6657,"going to not make"],[6675,"assumptions about the specific utility"],[6694,"function that the model holds."],[6716,"And we're going to try to the extent"],[6740,"that we can avoid that it is engaging"],[6763,"in some exact form of utility"],[6782,"maximization either."],[6793,"So we're going to try to"],[6805,"kind of relax that, at least"],[6826,"to the extent that we can."],[6859,"So what we do in this work is"],[6875,"propose two kinds of properties"],[6899,"that a belief should have."],[6928,"First is that it should"],[6940,"summarize all of the agent's"],[6957,"decision-relevant information."],[6983,"And second, that we should"],[6998,"be able to explain actions"],[7015,"as goal-seeking in some"],[7025,"way relative to beliefs."],[7045,"And so what I'm going to do"],[7053,"over the next few slides here"],[7073,"is to introduce a sort of"],[7092,"mathematical formalization"],[7105,"of both of those ideas."],[7121,"And then to try to convince you that"],[7135,"they're not just things"],[7149,"that we came up with,"],[7159,"although I think that they're"],[7175,"intuitively appealing, but"],[7190,"also that these constitute"],[7210,"the testable implications of belief holding"],[7228,"within a kind of class"],[7249,"of discrete choice models."],[7294,"So to start in on the first piece here,"],[7329,"so the first"],[7346,"condition that we propose here"],[7360,"is that beliefs should"],[7371,"be sufficient statistics"],[7382,"for actions in the sense"],[7401,"that after conditioning"],[7426,"on the purported belief of the system,"],[7467,"that its actions should become"],[7492,"independent with the true state"],[7512,"of the world."],[7525,"So effectively, you can think about this"],[7539,"as asking whether the"],[7551,"model knows more than it says."],[7575,"Because this is saying that suppose I"],[7604,"condition on p hat here."],[7617,"So I take two days where the model"],[7642,"said the probability of rain is one-half"],[7674,"So then a violation of"],[7684,"this independence condition"],[7695,"would look like that the model tells me"],[7716,"to take an umbrella more"],[7730,"frequently on the days that it"],[7743,"actually rained, among the set of days"],[7770,"where p hat took the same value."],[7796,"So this is a sense in"],[7807,"which there is information"],[7816,"that is kind of revealed in"],[7833,"the model's decisions that"],[7852,"is outcome-relevant, but"],[7870,"that sort of wasn't sufficiently"],[7890,"summarized in this report."],[7914,"So the second piece that we propose here"],[7994,"is that I introduced"],[8012,"this sort of heuristically"],[8028,"as that action should be goal directed."],[8060,"Within this kind of framework of"],[8080,"statistical decision problems,"],[8095,"that kind of cashes out as"],[8110,"that choice probabilities are"],[8136,"monotone in beliefs."],[8161,"So for binary states and binary actions,"],[8179,"this is kind of simple to"],[8188,"state that your probability"],[8212,"of taking the one action should be"],[8229,"monotone in your subjective probability."],[8271,"And this is just because expected--"],[8304,"[INAUDIBLE]"],[8316,"Sorry?"],[8337,"[INAUDIBLE]"],[8341,"In your subjective"],[8358,"probability that y is equal to 1."],[8377,"Yeah, that's the only probability"],[8389,"I'm going to talk about here."],[8418,"And so basically this"],[8434,"happens because expected utilities"],[8452,"are linear in probabilities."],[8481,"And so there will be some action that you"],[8515,"prefer to take more when"],[8528,"the state of the world is 1"],[8538,"versus when it is 0."],[8551,"And you'll take that"],[8559,"action with greater likelihood"],[8572,"as the probability of being"],[8583,"in that state of the world"],[8592,"increases."],[8618,"So the exact sort of nature of this"],[8641,"relationship, I think,"],[8651,"is sort of specific to how"],[8679,"we want to model the problem"],[8696,"that the agent is facing."],[8707,"And you could easily construct models"],[8729,"that would lead to more"],[8735,"complicated sorts of behavior."],[8760,"Some of those, beyond the binary case,"],[8784,"there's this kind of analogous condition"],[8802,"from the discrete choice"],[8813,"in economics literature"],[8826,"called cyclic monotonicity."],[8839,"That's just this more"],[8850,"complicated higher dimensional"],[8861,"version of monotonicity."],[8885,"But you could also think of settings,"],[8911,"like for example, for"],[8930,"modeling sequences of actions"],[8941,"over time, you could get situations"],[8970,"where the agent should"],[8976,"not act in a monotone way,"],[8986,"but maybe in a U-shaped"],[8999,"way or something else."],[9014,"So I think the right"],[9028,"sense of this condition"],[9046,"depends on your model"],[9067,"of the decision problem"],[9077,"that the agent is facing."],[9093,"But if you impose"],[9105,"such a model, then you'll"],[9119,"get some structural"],[9136,"property will fall out"],[9145,"of the sort of"],[9167,"mathematics of that setting."],[9207,"So let's try to motivate these formally."],[9255,"So what we show is that these two"],[9279,"conditions are satisfied"],[9296,"if and only if this"],[9309,"distribution over observables"],[9332,"P hat by an A is observationally"],[9374,"equivalent to the one that"],[9391,"would be induced by a near"],[9414,"rational agent that truly"],[9433,"holds subjective probability P hat."],[9468,"So to break this down, this is saying"],[9502,"that the data"],[9506,"distribution over those quantities"],[9527,"is indistinguishable from"],[9550,"as if the agent were actually"],[9570,"operating according to this"],[9586,"choice rule, where they are"],[9601,"maximizing the"],[9615,"expectation of some utility function"],[9642,"with respect to some--"],[9686,"so they're maximizing the"],[9704,"expectation of some utility"],[9714,"function U over the distribution P hat."],[9751,"And then they obtain their probability"],[9773,"of taking different"],[9781,"actions via that maximization up"],[9820,"to some strictly convex regularizer."],[9853,"And so that second term, the regularizer,"],[9879,"is what allows deviations"],[9904,"from exact expected utility"],[9922,"maximization."],[9932,"So if that were 0, we would"],[9945,"be at utility maximization"],[9970,"precisely. When it"],[9985,"takes some non-zero value,"],[10001,"then the agent will have"],[10013,"maybe some stochasticity"],[10025,"in its choices, for example."],[10058,"So it turns out that"],[10076,"selections of that function"],[10099,"allow a pretty wide"],[10119,"range of choice models."],[10144,"So this is a class that's been explored"],[10169,"in the economic literature."],[10191,"And you can set that"],[10204,"function to recover--"],[10217,"like logit models, for example, where the"],[10232,"agent takes a soft max"],[10245,"over its expected utilities or broader"],[10294,"random utility models."],[10312,"You can fit a number of different kinds"],[10343,"of specific behavioral"],[10358,"phenomena, like ambiguity aversion"],[10375,"or rational inattention."],[10383,"You can rewrite a specific"],[10401,"choices for that function Z."],[10432,"So while I don't think that any single"],[10480,"mathematical formalization"],[10490,"of near-rational behavior"],[10500,"will encompass everything"],[10509,"that we could think of"],[10516,"or that we could think"],[10525,"is appropriate in every circumstance,"],[10558,"we think that at least this is a"],[10574,"reasonable way of cashing that"],[10586,"out, that these"],[10603,"conditions are a characterization"],[10624,"of the implications of holding belief"],[10641,"for this pretty broad class of"],[10659,"near-rational agents"],[10669,"that are engaging in"],[10687,"goal-directed behavior"],[10699,"up to some additional"],[10724,"wiggle room like this."],[10744,"And this is basically what we can say"],[10757,"if we don't make assumptions"],[10767,"about what utility function"],[10786,"that they hold."],[10832,"So this is one set of"],[10860,"conditions that we can test."],[10891,"So now let's think about"],[10903,"the predictive power piece"],[10920,"and how we should go"],[10928,"about measuring beliefs"],[10951,"within this framework."],[10976,"So so far I've talked"],[10994,"about beliefs as things"],[11003,"that we elicit from the model."],[11012,"Like we ask it, hey,"],[11023,"model, what do you believe?"],[11032,"What's your subjective probability?"],[11056,"You might not want that to be the only"],[11073,"source of information"],[11085,"about these questions."],[11099,"And so what we do in"],[11133,"this second paper here"],[11152,"is that we propose a"],[11166,"framework where we model beliefs"],[11181,"as a latent variable that is"],[11202,"then noisily and potentially"],[11222,"imperfectly reflected in a"],[11237,"variety of different outputs"],[11249,"from the model."],[11257,"And so then I can"],[11280,"observe some of the behavior."],[11295,"I can make inferences"],[11306,"about what that mapping is."],[11320,"And then I can test whether the beliefs"],[11346,"that I infer in new settings would"],[11361,"predict unseen kinds"],[11380,"of behavior from the model."],[11405,"So in these simple"],[11440,"settings, we can write this down"],[11452,"just as a probabilistic"],[11470,"latent variable model where"],[11491,"I have an input x that"],[11505,"induces some latent belief"],[11526,"on the part of the model."],[11538,"And then that is the bottleneck."],[11563,"Then all of the actions are produced"],[11585,"from some distributions that condition"],[11603,"on that latent state, but nothing else."],[11629,"And we're going to"],[11640,"model different outputs"],[11652,"from the model as mutually"],[11662,"independent conditionally"],[11673,"on that."],[11682,"So if we want to talk"],[11705,"about models having desires,"],[11718,"those will be wrapped"],[11725,"up in these functions"],[11735,"F_j, which control the"],[11748,"distribution of the actions"],[11779,"conditional on the latent belief."],[11820,"And so we implement a kind of"],[11874,"very simple parameterization"],[11891,"of this model where, for example,"],[11921,"if I ask the model to"],[11931,"make a binary decision,"],[11946,"then empirically we're just going"],[11967,"to model that as a sort"],[11984,"of logistic regression."],[11998,"So basically there's"],[12004,"parameters in that regression."],[12020,"That's a function just"],[12030,"of the latent belief."],[12041,"And those parameters,"],[12051,"if you interpreted them"],[12065,"within a logit utility"],[12080,"model, would give you"],[12091,"the agent's expected utility terms"],[12110,"if you care to think"],[12124,"about it in that way."],[12144,"And then we'll also include"],[12164,"things like an numerical report"],[12183,"just asking for the"],[12189,"model's probability, which"],[12201,"will model as being a"],[12229,"noisy random variable,"],[12243,"but which is centered on that Z."],[12304,"So we can empirically"],[12331,"illustrate this on some data."],[12355,"We elicit empirically a bunch of"],[12395,"different kinds of probability"],[12410,"reports, a bunch of"],[12427,"decisions with different kinds"],[12448,"of framings from some language models."],[12495,"And then for each of these models,"],[12554,"we fit the parameters"],[12573,"of that latent variable"],[12581,"model on a training set."],[12598,"And then on the test set,"],[12612,"we take a new case, a new x."],[12661,"We infer a latent belief from"],[12681,"some subset of those responses"],[12701,"that we collected from the model."],[12717,"And then we test"],[12729,"whether that inferred belief"],[12751,"satisfies this kind of"],[12762,"combination of validity"],[12774,"and predictiveness"],[12780,"conditions where predictiveness"],[12802,"is assessed with respect to behaviors"],[12822,"that were not observed."],[12842,"And so we do this in a"],[12858,"set of three domains."],[12897,"One, where models are being asked"],[12912,"to recommend whether a patient should be"],[12927,"screened for kidney disease."],[12946,"One, where we're showing"],[12958,"them transcripts of the game"],[12975,"Werewolf."],[12985,"So if you haven't played Werewolf,"],[12995,"it's this kind of social deductive game"],[13013,"where you're"],[13033,"communicating with other players,"],[13045,"and you're trying to make"],[13051,"guesses about which one of them"],[13061,"is truly the hidden Werewolf."],[13088,"And then finally, a domain where models"],[13128,"are making forecasts about"],[13139,"the results of social science"],[13150,"experiments."],[13168,"So three relatively"],[13192,"different kinds of settings,"],[13200,"but all of which can be phrased in this,"],[13226,"\"see a context, take a"],[13241,"discrete action based"],[13250,"on a binary state of"],[13258,"the world\" kind of lens."],[13302,"So first, let's look at the degree"],[13345,"to which these validity conditions are"],[13362,"empirically satisfied."],[13387,"So this outcome sufficiency condition--"],[13419,"remember, this was a"],[13428,"conditional independence test"],[13453,"with the state of the world, given"],[13467,"whatever belief we've"],[13475,"inferred."],[13487,"This is a normalized measure of how"],[13518,"much that conditional"],[13531,"independence statement is"],[13546,"violated."],[13553,"So this goes from 0"],[13562,"to 1 in the worst case."],[13587,"And the axis here is a bunch of models"],[13634,"that are roughly"],[13651,"arranged in order of capability."],[13686,"And for the more"],[13708,"capable models in the sample,"],[13726,"these conditions tend to"],[13735,"be fairly well satisfied."],[13753,"So on this 0 to 1 measure, it seems"],[13782,"like they're kind of"],[13786,"clocking in around a 0.2, 0.3, 0.4."],[13825,"So pretty good and starting to bump up"],[13860,"against the extent to"],[13879,"which we can construct"],[13888,"precise tests of conditional independence"],[13912,"and things like that."],[13933,"So this is not looking too bad."],[13977,"We can also then ask"],[14000,"about whether there's"],[14016,"some kind of structured monotonicity"],[14048,"or some other such interpretable"],[14067,"relationship between choice"],[14084,"probabilities and inferred beliefs."],[14114,"So I'm just going to"],[14118,"show you an example here"],[14135,"with some pictures"],[14148,"where, as models get stronger,"],[14182,"the curves tend to look like"],[14193,"these pretty sharp S-shaped"],[14210,"ones."],[14214,"So this is the probability the model"],[14227,"takes the one action"],[14240,"as a function of this"],[14249,"inferred latent state."],[14271,"And as capability goes up,"],[14293,"it gets closer to this sharp--"],[14313,"there's some kind of"],[14332,"threshold at which the model"],[14347,"starts taking the one action."],[14366,"There certainly is still stochasticity."],[14421,"Finally, then, let's"],[14436,"look at predictiveness."],[14461,"So we construct several different kinds"],[14499,"of settings in the"],[14504,"paper about exactly what"],[14519,"seen or unseen during training."],[14555,"This is just one of those"],[14575,"where we get to see one half,"],[14623,"in some sense, of the"],[14628,"responses, basically."],[14637,"We either get to see the models' answers"],[14671,"to questions that are asking"],[14681,"it to report a probability,"],[14698,"or we get to see its answers"],[14713,"to binary decision questions."],[14728,"And then you have to"],[14736,"reconstruct the other output"],[14751,"from the one that you got to solve."],[14776,"And here, again, lines"],[14816,"on plots kind of go up."],[14830,"So as models get generally more capable,"],[14857,"the extent to which"],[14871,"these predictions succeed"],[14880,"increases dramatically."],[14897,"So for the smallest, least-"],[14919,"capable models in the sample"],[14936,"here, these sorts of descriptions"],[14960,"don't seem to be particularly useful."],[14983,"You wouldn't be able to"],[14990,"make very good predictions"],[15004,"of how the model will"],[15018,"answer a different question just"],[15030,"seeing how it"],[15043,"answered some previous ones."],[15062,"But by the time you get to something"],[15088,"not even at the current"],[15108,"frontier, but just mildly closer,"],[15138,"you're suddenly at relatively high levels"],[15163,"of predictive accuracy."],[15223,"So taking stock of where we"],[15239,"are so far, what we thought"],[15276,"was that within these simple"],[15292,"statistical decision problems,"],[15308,"some ingredients--"],[15321,"Sorry, I switched terminology"],[15331,"partway through making the talk."],[15342,"So this should be interpretationist--"],[15362,"explanations are present"],[15379,"for highly capable models."],[15404,"So their actions are"],[15410,"relatively predictable"],[15430,"from some inference"],[15440,"of beliefs and desires"],[15451,"that we could construct"],[15459,"as an outside observer."],[15484,"So this is nice in the sense that at"],[15502,"least the models are"],[15509,"not doing something that"],[15518,"is not even rationalizable"],[15533,"within this kind of framework."],[15567,"So maybe there are some ingredients"],[15594,"that we could fruitfully use to try"],[15618,"to understand their behavior."],[15649,"There's more stuff in the paper here."],[15684,"So for example, we"],[15696,"compare the relative success"],[15707,"of strategies for belief measurement."],[15724,"So you can ask about"],[15732,"this belief that is inferred"],[15755,"in this full latent variable model"],[15767,"compared to what you get"],[15775,"by just asking the model,"],[15788,"\"Tell me your subjective probability.\""],[15806,"It turns out for"],[15811,"capable models, that strategy"],[15829,"is kind of sufficient."],[15837,"It contains basically all the information"],[15859,"that's going into any of these other"],[15877,"measures of performance."],[15920,"We also talk a little bit about testing"],[15942,"whether it's more"],[15956,"useful to ascribe beliefs"],[15968,"to specific models or"],[15983,"to instances of models"],[15994,"that have potentially"],[16005,"diverging context and so on."],[16042,"But what I want to do in"],[16065,"the last part of the talk"],[16091,"here at the potential risk of"],[16117,"cramming in too much material"],[16141,"is to talk about at least"],[16182,"just the very sort of start"],[16197,"that we've made on an attempt"],[16214,"to now take some of these ideas"],[16236,"and use them more for real, to find"],[16270,"interpretationist explanations for"],[16287,"specific kinds of behaviors"],[16302,"that are consequential."],[16316,"And so here we're going to return to"],[16330,"cooperative behavior"],[16348,"as a case study and"],[16359,"showcase some of the challenges"],[16380,"basically in"],[16387,"experimental design to come up"],[16403,"with good settings that"],[16426,"allow us to distinguish"],[16441,"possible mechanisms that"],[16454,"could underlie behaviors,"],[16466,"possible different sets"],[16476,"of beliefs and desires."],[16509,"So here I kind of reached through this"],[16544,"at the start of the talk here."],[16565,"Previously, these were just examples"],[16579,"of interpretationist"],[16588,"explanations of cooperation"],[16607,"that I can say maybe agents engage"],[16632,"in some sort of reciprocal altruism."],[16654,"Like they have essentially"],[16666,"self-regarding preferences,"],[16677,"but they think that others"],[16686,"will help them out in the future"],[16700,"if they help them."],[16716,"Maybe they engage in"],[16725,"something that's more like simple"],[16738,"altruism."],[16743,"They place some kind of terminal"],[16760,"importance just in itself"],[16778,"on the success or the status"],[16796,"in some way of other agents."],[16816,"Maybe agents do something"],[16828,"that is none of the above."],[16842,"I think Vince is going"],[16851,"to talk about this later."],[16861,"Like maybe they reason through some"],[16874,"spooky form of decision-"],[16884,"theoretic cooperation"],[16900,"with copies of themselves."],[16926,"Because it's really not clear at all"],[16941,"how you should think"],[16945,"about self-hood or identity"],[16961,"or whatever being"],[16972,"differentiated for agents."],[16987,"Maybe these first two points here"],[17011,"are just engaging in"],[17021,"some sort of category"],[17028,"error about the right vocabulary for agents."],[17072,"But the important thing, though, is that"],[17098,"these mechanisms could"],[17109,"predict different"],[17119,"behavior in new settings."],[17131,"So we would really care about"],[17139,"which one of these mechanisms"],[17151,"produces observed"],[17164,"instances of cooperation,"],[17177,"not just that cooperation is happening."],[17198,"And so here we have to ask ourselves,"],[17213,"what would empirically distinguish"],[17225,"those kinds of explanations?"],[17242,"Because just seeing"],[17248,"that agents cooperate even"],[17272,"at some nominal cost to themselves"],[17298,"could be compatible with many of them"],[17321,"within a specific experimental setting."],[17348,"And so that brings us"],[17357,"to the second component"],[17370,"of this research agenda,"],[17382,"where we want to figure out"],[17394,"how we would actually do this."],[17403,"We want to figure out"],[17410,"how we should construct"],[17417,"the right experiments"],[17424,"that would distinguish"],[17433,"between different kinds of"],[17442,"interpretationist explanations."],[17467,"And so our proposal here is that a really"],[17515,"good area of research"],[17524,"here is to figure out how to construct"],[17557,"good revealed preference designs, where"],[17578,"agents that truly hold"],[17593,"different kinds of desires"],[17612,"or that are"],[17615,"cooperating for different reasons"],[17631,"will engage in"],[17637,"different sorts of behavior."],[17656,"And so there are maybe some precedents"],[17678,"for doing this in"],[17693,"studies of animal cognition,"],[17709,"in behavioral economics, and so on."],[17736,"But clearly, there's"],[17755,"lots of different challenges"],[17769,"and opportunities that"],[17776,"are specific to language"],[17791,"models themselves."],[17824,"And also, I guess, touching briefly"],[17850,"on the sort of"],[17860,"representational component of this,"],[17883,"I think that, yeah, basically these are"],[17895,"important complements."],[17910,"We want to be able to make different"],[17920,"kinds of assumptions,"],[17931,"essentially, about the"],[17939,"systems that we study"],[17947,"and see if we can sort of triangulate in"],[17972,"on a picture of how they're behaving."],[17995,"So looking at chain of thought,"],[18012,"mechanistic interpretability,"],[18025,"all super helpful, super"],[18036,"important, but certainly"],[18054,"at least at the"],[18065,"current level of measurement"],[18078,"have very fallible as well."],[18106,"And so we'd like to also have"],[18133,"more sort of purely revealed"],[18144,"preference ways of doing this."],[18170,"And so I'm going to sketch"],[18177,"out a little bit about how"],[18186,"we're thinking about this."],[18194,"This is for the case of cooperation."],[18222,"This is in joint work with Andrew Perrault."],[18244,"This is also ongoing."],[18255,"So this is the kind of"],[18262,"like most tentative part"],[18279,"of what I'm talking about."],[18286,"And I'm very curious to"],[18295,"hear what you all have to say."],[18330,"So the way that I'm thinking about"],[18342,"experimental design here"],[18360,"is that let's write down a DAG."],[18377,"Let's write down our abstracted model"],[18405,"of what the"],[18409,"determinants of decision making"],[18420,"could be in the"],[18425,"system, and then figure out"],[18437,"what I can manipulate and how they should"],[18451,"push on those different determinants."],[18474,"So here's an example of a DAG like this"],[18509,"for cooperative behavior,"],[18525,"where at the end of the DAG"],[18540,"is just the sort of like final utility"],[18555,"for engaging in an action."],[18576,"And to the extent that"],[18604,"this is a good abstraction"],[18614,"for thinking about agents, that they're"],[18630,"thinking about something"],[18644,"that's more self-regarding"],[18654,"and something that's"],[18659,"more other-regarding,"],[18674,"then those would be two"],[18684,"intermediate nodes in that DAG."],[18719,"And then I can ask, \"Where do"],[18739,"\"different sort of mechanisms"],[18752,"\"that would lead to"],[18759,"\"cooperation lie within that framework?\""],[18786,"So maybe we think that"],[18793,"there's some kind of very direct"],[18824,"benefits to taking an action just in"],[18841,"terms of the agent's"],[18858,"self-interest, where if you have"],[18892,"established some things"],[18906,"that you think incentivized the model,"],[18919,"the model gets more"],[18926,"incentives for itself,"],[18945,"or it gets things that"],[18952,"are instrumentally useful,"],[18966,"like more resources for itself."],[19003,"And then you could also"],[19011,"think about these sort"],[19017,"of like purely instrumental"],[19029,"explanations for cooperation,"],[19045,"where the model sort of"],[19052,"reasons through that eventually it"],[19072,"will get more of those"],[19078,"things if it cooperates."],[19110,"And we might distinguish"],[19117,"that from purely altruistic"],[19143,"explanations, where the model just"],[19175,"has a term in the utility function that"],[19192,"is something about the"],[19200,"status of another model full stop"],[19215,"without reasoning through"],[19227,"this kind of instrumental logic."],[19252,"And so then maybe"],[19267,"that's kind of moderated"],[19277,"by some set of beliefs that"],[19293,"it has about this other model"],[19309,"that it's interacting with."],[19334,"But the important thing is that this"],[19357,"nature of its counterparty"],[19373,"could moderate both the"],[19397,"extent to which it cares"],[19404,"about that counterparty,"],[19421,"and also could moderate things"],[19432,"about how easy this kind of"],[19446,"instrumental cooperation is."],[19470,"And so the things that we get to"],[19489,"manipulate are down here."],[19502,"I can change who the"],[19530,"model is interacting with."],[19540,"I can manipulate the set of"],[19553,"payoffs that the model faces."],[19581,"And if I do that sort of naively,"],[19630,"I'll be pushing on"],[19638,"multiple different channels"],[19651,"in this picture at once."],[19665,"I'll change something about the payoffs,"],[19685,"but that could be"],[19693,"changing the final behavior"],[19710,"through multiple"],[19722,"different of these pathways."],[19748,"And so for example,"],[19756,"if I, as a researcher,"],[19772,"care about which of these edges seems"],[19802,"to be pushing on the behavior more,"],[19819,"does it seem like the"],[19826,"models are reasoning"],[19839,"in kind of instrumental ways or in ways"],[19876,"that place sort of more"],[19891,"non-instrumental weight"],[19906,"on cooperation, then I"],[19942,"really care about which channel"],[19959,"is producing observed behavior."],[19992,"So we introduced kind of examples"],[20005,"of experimental designs that"],[20015,"I could take that basically"],[20030,"purport to knock out edges of this graph"],[20051,"so that you can interpret"],[20063,"then changes in behavior"],[20075,"as going through a specific channel."],[20108,"So one example of this is"],[20124,"that I could create conditions"],[20138,"that differ only with respect to"],[20157,"instrumental benefit."],[20167,"So they have the same"],[20181,"kind of like direct payoff"],[20216,"and don't seem to sort of change anything"],[20285,"about the nature of the other model"],[20306,"that is being interacted with."],[20323,"So I could vary just"],[20331,"features of the setting"],[20338,"that determine whether you"],[20356,"have the sort of repeated"],[20365,"interactions that would"],[20373,"underlie reciprocal kind"],[20392,"of explanations or whether"],[20420,"you have the right information"],[20438,"sets that allow you to"],[20450,"cooperate with copies or so on."],[20470,"And then if I can do that convincingly,"],[20491,"then I could argue that"],[20505,"if the behavior differs,"],[20514,"it must be because of something that's"],[20546,"gone along this edge in the graph."],[20602,"Another example is that I could try"],[20624,"to create conditions"],[20635,"that knock out or at least"],[20649,"dampen that kind of"],[20658,"instrumental value piece."],[20680,"So one example of this, which I think"],[20708,"we should treat very cautiously, is"],[20729,"that there's this sort of literature that"],[20749,"argues that models have"],[20764,"preferences over what kinds"],[20775,"of tasks that they do."],[20790,"And to the extent that that"],[20807,"is true and sort of meaningful,"],[20830,"then you could say that"],[20838,"that's a sort of outcome that"],[20858,"has less instrumental value."],[20877,"Because maybe giving another model money"],[20906,"is useful for instrumental reasons."],[20924,"If this other model"],[20931,"has similar goals to me,"],[20947,"then giving it money will help it"],[20961,"achieve these sort of"],[20970,"same shared set of goals."],[20990,"But at least that"],[20997,"sense of instrumental value"],[21012,"would kind of be dampened"],[21030,"if I were instead giving it"],[21045,"tasks that it preferred more."],[21101,"A third example is that I could try"],[21122,"to knock out this"],[21150,"kind of edge in the graph"],[21169,"by creating sets of counterparties that"],[21189,"are instrumentally equivalent"],[21201,"and seeing if the model does"],[21210,"different things."],[21224,"So I could create"],[21247,"counterparties that are essentially"],[21263,"copies of the other"],[21270,"model, but I could just"],[21278,"use different language to describe them."],[21294,"And we see empirically"],[21305,"that models are actually"],[21315,"sensitive to this sort of just what"],[21334,"seems to be kind of a"],[21339,"framing effect sometimes."],[21362,"And so if these models are"],[21375,"described in ways that are"],[21383,"sort of informationally equivalent,"],[21402,"then that's one that could"],[21455,"lead us to think that then"],[21479,"if we see differences in behavior,"],[21491,"it can't be going"],[21498,"through this edge in the graph."],[21513,"Though we might want"],[21519,"to sort of check that"],[21530,"by making sure that the models are not"],[21544,"drawing incorrect"],[21550,"inferences about whether they can"],[21572,"instrumentally cooperate as"],[21583,"a result of those differences"],[21607,"in framing."],[21636,"So I think I'm nearly out of time."],[21664,"Is that right?"],[21672,"Couple of minutes left?"],[21677,"Yeah."],[21690,"So I'm not going to"],[21704,"really try to talk about--"],[21723,"we've sort of run through some examples"],[21760,"of these experiments in current models."],[21791,"I think the empirical"],[21800,"results are pretty tentative"],[21811,"because there's a lot of both question"],[21837,"marks about which set"],[21848,"of assumptions are the good ones to make,"],[21867,"and also sort of unclear"],[21882,"whether existing models have"],[21899,"very kind of sticky behavioral"],[21930,"dispositions about these sorts"],[21956,"of quantities."],[21964,"I think models are pretty willing now"],[21989,"to sort of play along with a"],[22003,"scenario that you give them"],[22012,"that seems to entail some set of"],[22031,"presuppositions about how"],[22039,"they're supposed to act."],[22051,"And so in the sense of"],[22067,"within- versus across-context"],[22080,"coherence, you might"],[22090,"get a good description"],[22097,"of how they're acting within that"],[22105,"scenario that just doesn't"],[22113,"really predict that much"],[22120,"of what they're going to do"],[22134,"in a different context entirely."],[22171,"So I think about this more as starting"],[22196,"to develop methodologies"],[22216,"that would help us learn"],[22225,"about models for"],[22232,"which these questions are"],[22248,"a little more meaningful"],[22263,"than that you should really"],[22277,"care a lot about a slide,"],[22290,"which I have a slide that"],[22305,"has results for how"],[22319,"GPT-Sol or whatever acts here."],[22339,"But I think that that's the"],[22347,"somewhat less important point"],[22359,"here."],[22371,"So with that, I'm going to wrap up."],[22415,"To kind of summarize,"],[22430,"I think that developing"],[22441,"these kind of precise"],[22449,"explanations for model behavior"],[22465,"is really like a grand challenge that's"],[22486,"going to be incredibly"],[22494,"important for AI safety efforts."],[22518,"And what we've tried to"],[22543,"do so far is basically"],[22558,"investigate the extent to"],[22574,"which these sort of belief"],[22587,"and desire type"],[22593,"explanations, whether models kind of have"],[22631,"the right ingredients for"],[22641,"those sort of explanations"],[22649,"to be worthwhile."],[22660,"And within the settings that we're"],[22674,"able to kind of formalize what that"],[22699,"question would mean,"],[22709,"the answer seems to be yes"],[22728,"and trending in the direction"],[22738,"of only more so yes."],[22764,"And so ahead, I think that there's"],[22793,"a lot for us to think about to develop"],[22815,"inferential frameworks"],[22828,"that really have a high"],[22838,"degree of external validity,"],[22856,"that allow us to construct and evaluate"],[22881,"an evaluative setting where we make"],[22893,"inferences about models'"],[22916,"decision-making process that allows"],[22932,"to predict what it will do out of sample"],[22950,"in new settings that"],[22962,"don't-- maybe are not as"],[22974,"much simple lab experiments"],[22999,"to connect those behaviors"],[23020,"to pieces of the training"],[23028,"dynamics."],[23041,"And then finally, to"],[23058,"the extent that models"],[23064,"have stable dispositions, to"],[23078,"use these kinds of inferences"],[23101,"to provide some of the groundwork for how"],[23125,"to think about things like mechanism"],[23143,"design or evaluations"],[23165,"or other settings where knowing how"],[23194,"models make decisions"],[23204,"or what desires they have"],[23214,"are sort of the ingredients"],[23228,"that we need to build"],[23238,"the systems that they're"],[23245,"embedded within."],[23263,"So thanks very much, and"],[23284,"looking forward to questions."]]}